[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_item")
id = "book_hallam"
display_name = "Hallam and the Hundred Lights"
description = "A children's songbook, soft with handling, from the waystation."
value = 5
weight = 0.5
book_text = "Inside the cover, in a child's careful capitals: TOBIN'S. NOT YOURS. NOT EVEN MAMS.

HALLAM AND THE HUNDRED LIGHTS
(to be sung at Lanternfast, with the shutters closed)

When the lights came down they were many and bright,
and they crept through the shutters in the dead of the night,
and they drank the warm breath of the children asleep,
so Hallam the Lamplighter went out to keep watch.

(Tobin has crossed out \"to keep watch\" and written \"with his sheep\". Underneath, in a grown-up hand: IT IS NOT ABOUT SHEEP, TOBIN.)

He took up his lantern, he took up his hook,
he went to the stones where the lights used to look,
and he caught one each night, and he put out its glow,
for a hundred nights more, through the rain and the snow.

On the hundredth night, by the old standing stone,
the last light was little, and frightened, and alone.
It said, \"We were lost, and we only came by,\"
and Hallam said, \"You should have stayed in the sky.\"

So light your lantern and shutter it tight,
and sleep, little one, through the dark of the night,
for Hallam is watching, his hook at his side,
and no light gets in where a lantern's inside."
teaches_skill = "archery"
